+
+Seeded policy `observation-corpus-v1` is a fixed, non-learning action policy. At step t, seat s, actor ordinal a, choose the unit command indexed by `(t+s+a)%8` from `[PASS, NORTH, SOUTH, EAST, WEST, PLANT(WHEAT), WATER, HARVEST]`. Emit farmer and **every current hand** explicitly in their engine order. One market queue entry indexed by `(t+s)%6`: `[HIRE]`, `[BUY_SEED,WHEAT,1]`, `[BUY_PRODUCT,WHEAT,1]`, `[SELL,WHEAT,1]`, `[BUY_LAND]`, `[]` (empty order). One entry never exceeds M. Engine decides unsuccessful actions; no hidden affordability repair or bot import. Store a SHA-256 of the exact ordered JSON action stream per seed, final snapshot hash and sampled steps. Replay it from seed in the producer test; do not call any reference `TrainingBatch`.
+
+For each dense index d=0..31, clone a snapshot of profile 2, set step `d*3` (<=93), recompute day/hour, unlock NW/NE/SW/SE and place 240 hands per farm with actor i at `[(i+d+3*s)%10, ((i/10)+2*d+s)%10]`; no invalid y=23 copied from the reference's old dense test. Populate 241 inventories per seat in rotated Item order `(j+i+d+s)%12`, counts `(i+3*j+d+s)%37`, with present-zero keys and absent-key cases. Alternate shift-remove/reinsert of WHEAT at equal count in paired d values; ensure at least one pair differs only in insertion order. Do the same for sheds, plus separate replacement-without-removal controls. Use multiplier 0 when hires=240; include lower, unequal public hires for positive-cost cases. Maintain finite banks, market default params and in-range cells. Add all five crops, all three animals, EMPTY/LOCKED/WEED/empty structures, positive/zero yields, -1 sentinels, overdue deadlines, ever-but-no-longer fertilized, pending bonus and duplicate shop types. Cover each enum in both perspectives. Full-capacity states use M=10 in dedicated dense records; zero multiplier permits the 241+241 state to remain representable. Pin exact dense-case recipes in source and list their tags/coverage in the manifest; no random rejection sampling.
