+| Test family | Oracle / negative control |
+|---|---|
+| L4 tagged decimals | literal .125/1.75/.625; fails with unification and unpatched enum; all existing Orbit fixtures retained |
+| Config/representability | accepted contract + engine Config rules; i64 extremes, fractional market, finite-f64/nonfinite-f32; no normalization ceilings |
+| Tiles | hand-computed asymmetric cells, integer/sentinel fields, gating and fertilizer distinctions; deliberate gate/transpose mutations |
+| Actor/storage/ranks | parsed engine IndexMap order, zero-vs-absent, shift_remove/reinsert vs replacement; final (241st) actor; >2^24 counts |
+| Public context/hire/order limit | engine process_market/do_hire and literal Fibonacci; custom clock/interval/weed profiles; unequal rival hires |
+| Buffer binding | dtype/shape/contiguity/alias mutations, poisoned bytes, stable pointers, two-env late failure |
+| Privacy/role order | each rival-private mutation leaves opposite row exact but changes own row; complete seat swap |
+| Corpus custody | hashes/strict schema/counts/quotas + deliberate byte corruption and reordered records/seat blocks |
+| Information preservation | pinned reference encode_invest, all 8,176 slots, 512 states × both seats, exact f32 bits and offset coverage |
+| Added facts | independent state checks and paired states with equal legacy vectors but changed insertion order/new config values |
+| Python schema | actual Task 2.1 class on every emitted corpus batch, no duplicate class or silent skip |
+| Reuse/Rayon/transaction | dense→sparse full overwrite, serial=2-worker bytes, invalid final env never publishes first env |
+| Access cost | one-snapshot counter and bounded phase timings, not training/GPU performance |
